      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Defect** — The return value of `flash_ex_op` is ignored. If reading the status register fails (e.g., due to an SPI error), `sr[0]` and `sr[1]` will remain uninitialized. Later in `cros_flash_rtkfp_init`, this garbage data will be modified and written back to the flash chip, which could lock the chip into an unpredictable protection state.\n\nPlease change this function to return an `int` and propagate the error:\n\n```c\nstatic int flash_get_status(const struct device *dev, uint8_t *sr1, uint8_t *sr2)\n{\n\tconst struct cros_flash_rtkfp_config *cfg \u003d DRV_CONFIG(dev);\n\tuint8_t sr[2];\n\tint rv;\n\n\tcrec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(1);\n\trv \u003d flash_ex_op(cfg-\u003eflash_dev, FLASH_RTS5817_EX_OP_RD_SR, (uintptr_t)NULL,\n\t\t         sr);\n\tcrec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(0);\n\n\tif (rv \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\t*sr1 \u003d sr[0];\n\t\t*sr2 \u003d sr[1];\n\t}\n\n\treturn rv;\n}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/d037d9a5-f6b3-4a33-8322-0a86a2e32ead)",
